Build a Plan of Action and Milestones (POA&M)
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Deploy a lightweight ticketing system to track remediation findings
Convert Security Assessment Report (SAR) findings into structured, trackable tickets
Assign ownership, severity, milestones, and target close dates to findings
Document risk acceptance decisions and residual risk levels
Export a POA&M report in OSCAL-compliant JSON format
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command-line familiarity (package management, file editing)
Understanding of vulnerability/finding severity ratings (Critical/High/Medium/Low)
Conceptual knowledge of NIST RMF (Domain 5: Authorization, Domain 7: Continuous Monitoring)
No prior Redmine or OSCAL experience required
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a single Linux machine (Ubuntu 22.04) via Start Lab. All work is done locally — no external cloud accounts needed.

